{"archetypes":[{"name":"orphan-var-cleanup","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan removes three separate orphaned variable resolutions across three different files; a partial deletion in any one file silently trips shellcheck SC2034 and fails make lint without a clear cross-file audit.","prompt_body":"The plan removes `WORKFLOW_PATH` from `design-postplan-emit.sh`, `_wp_round` from `run-step3-review.sh`, `design_classification` from `assess-plan-round.sh`, and the `--design-classification` arg from `design-plan-quality-assessor.sh`'s invocation of `assess-plan-round.sh`. Verify the plan's deletion instructions cover every usage of each orphaned symbol within its target file — a residual reference still triggers shellcheck SC2034 and fails `make lint` even if the primary gate is deleted. Confirm the plan correctly preserves the legitimate `WORKFLOW_PATH` usage inside `design-plan-quality-assessor.sh` for the `.step3.6-assessor.env` write, and that this surviving usage is not accidentally swept up by the orphan-cleanup instructions. Check for asymmetric caller/callee gaps: specifically whether removing `--design-classification` from the caller is mentioned in the same plan section that removes the arg parser from the callee, or whether one side is left dangling. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"round1-prompt-coherence","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan sets plan_prev=plan_original on round 1 but does not fully address how render-assessor-prompt.sh handles duplicate identical inputs in its three-section template, which could yield ambiguous or wrong BETTER/WORSE/TIE verdicts.","prompt_body":"The plan sets `plan_prev = plan_original` on round 1 in `assess-plan-round.sh` because no `plan-after-round-0.txt` exists yet, then passes both as separate arguments to `render-assessor-prompt.sh`, which renders three named sections: `## Original plan (anchor)`, `## Previous round plan`, and `## Current round plan`. Verify the plan explicitly describes what the rendered prompt looks like when the original and previous-round inputs point to the same file — identical content in two sections may confuse the assessor model into a TIE verdict even when the current plan has genuinely regressed. Check whether the re-anchoring instruction change planned for `render-assessor-prompt.sh` is sufficient for the round-1 case, or whether the prompt template needs an explicit note distinguishing the round-1 degenerate case from a true multi-round comparison. Confirm that `test-render-assessor-prompt.sh` is expected to add an assertion specifically for the round-1 identical-inputs shape, and flag if the plan omits this. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-gap","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan lists seven harness files to update but defers the snapshot-plan-round.sh harness check to a vague 'verify no change needed' note and does not enumerate which stale tier-skip assertions must be removed to avoid false-passing tests.","prompt_body":"The plan adds new assertions across seven harness files (SIMPLE snapshot `taken`/`preserved`, SIMPLE round-cursor advance, SIMPLE assessor-lane banner and env output, round-1 WORSE-majority regression, render-assessor-prompt unified-anchor) but does not enumerate which existing tier-skip or `skipped-not-hard` or `--design-classification` assertions must be deleted — stale assertions that still pass will give false confidence that the old behavior is preserved. Verify the plan explicitly targets each obsolete assertion for removal in the same edit that adds the replacement, and check whether `test-assess-plan-round.sh` retains any SIMPLE-must-skip or `workflow_path-vs-classification` fixture that now contradicts the tier-agnostic behavior. Examine the plan's deferred handling of `test-snapshot-plan-round.sh`: it says 'verify no change needed beyond any HARD-only fixture comment' without naming what to look for, which is a coverage gap rather than a confirmed no-op. Confirm the round-1 WORSE-majority regression in `test-assess-plan-round.sh` mirrors the existing `setup_round2` WORSE stub pattern at round 1 with no `plan-after-round-0.txt` present, so it exercises the new anchor path rather than accidentally falling through to the missing-input guard. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
